{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Keep on Dreaming"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tag questions</span> are used to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are used when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not</span>. </li><li><span class=\"strong\">  to encourage a reply </span>from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li vale=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive </span>statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative </span>question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes'. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were </span>stressed, <span class=\"strong\">weren't </span>you?</li><li> You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> looking for work, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you? </li><li> She<span class=\"strong\"> has </span>a degree, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't </span>she? </li><li> He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak Spanish, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative </span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive </span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> You <span class=\"strong\">weren't </span> stressed, <span class=\"strong\"> were </span>you?</li> <li> You <span class=\"strong\">aren't </span> looking for work, <span class=\"strong\"> are </span> you? </li> <li> She <span class=\"strong\"> doesn't </span> have a degree, <span class=\"strong\"> does </span> she? </li><li> He <span class=\"strong\"> can't </span> speak Spanish, <span class=\"strong\"> can </span> he? </li></ul></span></li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. For the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> the tag will be the auxiliary verb <span class=\"strong\">have </span> or <span class=\"strong\">has</span>. For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\"> do/does </span> or <span class=\"italic\"> did/didn't</span>. Look at the examples in the chart."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":13,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Aren't I?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"haven't I?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hasn't she?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, you aren't working yet, are you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "That is a publishing house, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You've heard of them, haven't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You talked to them, didn't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm the boss, aren't I?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">reported speech</span> when you are saying (reporting)  what other people said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">reported speech</span> when we want to repeat what someone had previously said. </br>You need to change the verb to the next past form. This is called back-sliding. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Direct speech </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Reported speech </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Robert: \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">worked </span> there\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> had worked</span> there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Kelly: \\\"I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming </span>to lunch.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She said she <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> was coming </span> to lunch.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Coworkers: \\\"We already <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> finished</span>.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They said they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already </span>finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mark: \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can </span> type.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> could </span> type.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mindy: \\\"Where do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> study</span>?\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> studied</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have to change the <span class=\"strong\">pronoun</span> if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"<ul> <li> I said, \"I don't want to go.\" > I said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I </span> </span> didn't want to go. </li><li> Tina said, \"I don't want to go.\" > Tina said <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> she </span> </span> didn't want to go."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do you mean where have I been?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What did they say?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The director said that they are going to hire an editor assistant and they liked my qualifications."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My friend Davis heard that BFP had a good standing as an up-and-coming company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to <span class=\"strong\">report questions</span> asked, the <span class=\"strong\">subject </span> normally comes before the <span class=\"strong\">verb</span>. <br> Example: <br> Direct: \"Where are they?\" <br> Indirect: He asked me where they were."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When the question is a yes/no questions, you use <span class=\"strong\">if</span> or <span class=\"strong\">whether </span> to report it. <br> Example: <br> Direct: \"Is that the report?\" <br> Indirect: She asked me if that was the report. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They asked whether there was a new editor hired yet."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The interviewer asked me when I had graduated from school."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sounds like a plan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that's a good idea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Let's meet Thursday? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Sounds like a plan."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are gathering information about a company."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up-and-coming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "promising; has a lot of potential for growth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My friend Davis heard that BFP is an up-and-coming company."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "good standing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a solid or well established position compared to others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  BFP has a good standing as an in the publishing world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "by the way"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " an expression showing you are about to give an additional piece of related information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  By the way, Adam always asks what you have been doing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lend a hand"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "help"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Adam is going to lend a hand as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I visit employment websites and search them efficiently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze information and compare it to a criteria (my job skills)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a description of why this job could be suitable for me."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare my ideas and give feedback."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Visit a popular employment website to search for positions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Put in a few keywords for jobs that you would like. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose two jobs from the list of positions you have found that you would like to apply for. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you can't find one then create your own job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make sure to choose jobs that match your skills in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The jobs do not need to be identical to the jobs you have had in the past, or to the subject you are studying at school. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph for each job explaining why those jobs would match your skill set. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare with a partner and give feedback."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for confirmation. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss future plans."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report what someone had previously said."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How many job interviews have you been to?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What kinds of questions did they ask you?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Preparing for a job interview!"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Maybe one of your co-workers has a car you can borrow. You should <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">ask around</span>."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback":